## 13. Design Diagrams

### 13.1 High-Level Architecture

```mermaid
graph TD
    User[User / Teams / Web] -->|SSO| EVA[EVA Initiator]
    EVA --> Planner[Planner Agent A2A]

    Planner -->|Select & Orchestrate| ARS[Agent Registry Service]
    Planner -->|Dispatch Job| DBX[Databricks Jobs]

    DBX --> Agent1[ServiceNow Agent]
    DBX --> Agent2[UC Catalog Agent]
    DBX --> AgentN[Other Domain Agents]

    Agent1 --> Planner
    Agent2 --> Planner
    AgentN --> Planner

    Planner --> Response[Final Synthesized Response]
    Response --> User

    Planner --> Logs[MLflow + UC Logs]
    Planner --> Feedback[Feedback Service]
```

---

### 13.2 Query Processing Sequence

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
    participant U as User
    participant E as EVA Initiator
    participant P as Planner Agent
    participant R as Agent Registry
    participant D as Databricks Job
    participant A as Sub-Agent

    U->>E: User Query
    E->>P: Session + Query Context
    P->>R: Fetch Authorized Agents
    R-->>P: Agent Metadata
    P->>D: Dispatch Job
    D->>A: Execute Agent Logic
    A-->>D: Structured Result
    D-->>P: Agent Output
    P-->>U: Final Response
```

---

### 13.3 Agent Registration Flow (Dev → Stage → Prod)

```mermaid
flowchart LR
    Creator[Agent Creator] --> ARSDev[ARS Dev]
    ARSDev -->|Register| DevDBX[Dev Databricks]

    ARSDev -->|Promote| ARSStg[ARS Stage]
    ARSStg --> StgDBX[Stage Databricks]

    ARSStg -->|Promote| ARSProd[ARS Prod]
    ARSProd --> ProdDBX[Prod Databricks]
```

---

### 13.4 Planner vs Agent Responsibility Boundary

```mermaid
flowchart TB
    Planner[Planner Agent]
    Agent[Sub-Agent]

    Planner -->|Select Agent| Agent
    Planner -->|Dispatch Job| Agent
    Planner -->|Store Memory Ref| Memory[(Memory Index)]

    Agent -->|Read Memory| Memory
    Agent -->|Execute Tools| Tools[(APIs / Systems)]
    Agent -->|Return Structured Output| Planner
```

---

## 14. Summary

This document defines EVA as a **platform-grade agent orchestration system** with:

* A strict **planner-as-controller** model
* Registry-driven agent lifecycle (dev → stage → prod)
* Databricks-first execution using jobs
* Clear separation of control, execution, memory, and UI
* Strong foundations for security, observability, and scale

This version is considered the **final baseline design** for implementation, reviews, and roadmap alignment.
